      "title": "START HERE \u2014 4K local repair instructions",
      "properties": {
        "widget_ue_connectable": {}
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "4K LOCAL REPAIR \u2014 FLUX.2 KLEIN REFERENCE + MASK\n\n1. In LOAD FINISHED 4K IMAGE, choose/upload the image you want to repair.\n2. Right-click it \u2192 Open in MaskEditor. Paint white ONLY over the pixels that may change, then Save to node.\n3. Rewrite the green EDIT PROMPT so it says what must appear inside the mask.\n4. Queue. The workflow crops only the repair area, edits that crop, and stitches it back at the exact original resolution.\n5. Use the Before / After slider to inspect the result. The saved file is in output/4K-Local-Repair-V2.\n\nMASKING\n\u2022 Hand: paint the entire malformed hand/fingers and a tiny part of the wrist. Keep most wrist/forearm/watch unmasked as anchors.\n\u2022 Smile: paint lips plus a small area around the mouth; do not mask the whole face.\n\u2022 Remove object/person: paint the full object and a narrow border around it.\n\nDENOISE (KSampler)\n\u2022 0.50\u20130.62: expression or tiny detail\n\u2022 0.68\u20130.78: reconstruct a hand (default 0.72)\n\u2022 0.85\u20131.00: remove or replace a large object\n\nThis V2 uses the original crop twice: as the starting latent and as FLUX.2's reference latent. The mask is attached as the noise mask, so unpainted crop pixels remain structural anchors. Crop-and-Stitch restores the untouched 4K pixels afterward."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "4K LOCAL REPAIR \u2014 FLUX.2 KLEIN REFERENCE + MASK\n\n1. In LOAD FINISHED 4K IMAGE, choose/upload the image you want to repair.\n2. Right-click it \u2192 Open in MaskEditor. Paint white ONLY over the pixels that may change, then Save to node.\n3. Rewrite the green EDIT PROMPT so it says what must appear inside the mask.\n4. Queue. The workflow crops only the repair area, edits that crop, and stitches it back at the exact original resolution.\n5. Use the Before / After slider to inspect the result. The saved file is in output/4K-Local-Repair-V2.\n\nMASKING\n\u2022 Hand: paint the entire malformed hand/fingers and a tiny part of the wrist. Keep most wrist/forearm/watch unmasked as anchors.\n\u2022 Smile: paint lips plus a small area around the mouth; do not mask the whole face.\n\u2022 Remove object/person: paint the full object and a narrow border around it.\n\nDENOISE (KSampler)\n\u2022 0.50\u20130.62: expression or tiny detail\n\u2022 0.68\u20130.78: reconstruct a hand (default 0.72)\n\u2022 0.85\u20131.00: remove or replace a large object\n\nThis V2 uses the original crop twice: as the starting latent and as FLUX.2's reference latent. The mask is attached as the noise mask, so unpainted crop pixels remain structural anchors. Crop-and-Stitch restores the untouched 4K pixels afterward."
      },
      "color": "#243",
      "bgcolor": "#465"
    },
